  "verdict": "SUPPORTED_MOBILIZATION_WRITER_PHASE_EXACT_BRANCH_UNMEASURED",
  "summary": "Source and retained n84 records support turn-22 ongoing-mobilization as the positive writer phase for pale:RS before regular reinforcement opens at available111. This is an exclusive-path deduction under the observed canonical OSID battle path, not a literal pool-write receipt. Direct RS controller credit versus shared displaced-in credit, gross amounts/operands and any subsequent pool decay remain UNMEASURED. No gameplay defect or allocation fix is established.",
  "proof": "The measured interval is turn21 regular close0/1600 to turn22 regular open111/1600. Initial Pale wounded_pending is0. Militia casualties are the sole positive pending producer; the canonical OSID battle resolver emits defender_militia_pool_key and the scenario runner forwards that key into the retained weekly battle ledger. Zero pale:RS militia battle rows through22 therefore exclude turn21 WIA trickleback, provided that canonical projection is complete for this run. This is the explicit source-and-ledger assumption. Other bounded alternatives are nonpositive, gated by an already-active sole authored Pale brigade/player_choice mode, or the observed takeover arrival24 with floor-zero one-turn credit. Ongoing mobilization remains the surviving positive phase; decay can reduce its gross credit before available111 is observed.",
  "boundary": "Retained weekly artifacts omit the relevant phase reports, and the personnel observer records brigade strength rather than pool balances. Pale pool before/after values and actual exhaustion, displaced-in, controller/modifier and decay operands are absent at the credit/debit boundaries. Source formulas, numeric coincidences and synthetic/replayed reconstructions do not establish the missing branch-level write. No n80 counterfactual or historical cause is recovered.",
  "validation": "822-A extraction exited child/wrapper0/0. 822-B and822-C finalizers each exited1/126, respectively at takeover-displacement and phase-key assertions, with result.json absent. The final frozen822 synthesis was written outside a successful finalizer receipt; its hash identifies the reviewed text, and must not be described as finalizer0/0. All three receipts, snapshots and failures remain intact. Independent823 review supplies the explicit WIA exclusion and accepts the writer phase with these provenance qualifications. This new824 synthesis is generated in its own preserved wrapper, without erasing the earlier gap or claiming a rerun.",
  "next_action": "Smallest justified next fix is observability only: a default-off, stdout-only receipt selected for pale:RS and completed turns21–22, using the existing selector. Capture before/after balances, reached gates and actual direct/shared mobilization and decay operands across the relevant chain, including inherited close/WIA qualification/recruitment/reroute/spawn/regular-open continuity. Do not instrument every municipality or repository writer. Prove selector isolation, source access order and default-off neutrality with focused producer/reader tests and independent review before proposing any separately authorized measurement. No gameplay/threshold change, observer implementation or new campaign is authorized by this diagnosis.",
  "preservation": "Production/source, tests, reader, threshold/reference and C/D telemetry hashes remain exact; telemetry append0. C103894385/00d6d7e65832a45e4b8ddc34e077c228b9496ca8f1068a6b9633571b4bae5557; D1041/ff120d4aab551ad703cac3b1dc260d71cab1464b9bf5a57dba76c86baf3346e3. No campaign, replay, runTurn, build or full suite. Retained n80 703/712 remains NO-GO/unadopted, rejected n83/n84 trajectory unchanged and all inherited acceptance gates remain.",
